    "created_at": "2018-11-15T14:53:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-11-15T14:53:57Z",
    "body": "You mean the disadvantage that authors can't use \"`[orient=vertical]`\" as a selector?\r\nThat seems like a non-issue if the orientation is specified in CSS by the author since presumably they already have a relevant selector for those elements.  CSS is better since this **is** a rendering concern and it allows you to easily switch between horizontal/vertical layout based on media queries etc. Still, I guess we could have a HTML attribute too and simply attribute-map it to the CSS property. I just don't think it's needed.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
