    "created_at": "2019-01-25T14:49:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-01-25T14:49:49Z",
    "body": "> I'd be happy if UA can detect orientation with DOM level information such as content attribute because the current range implementation in Blink uses shadow nodes and updating shadow nodes style depending on the host style needs a hack.\r\n\r\nIs that just an implementation issue in Blink or is it a more fundamental design error in Shadow DOM? It seems kind of sad to me if Shadow DOM implies that we're going back to styling things using HTML attributes instead of CSS.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
